body:
It shouldn't be a rendering server issue.

I don't think `NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE` will emit on a script when performing C# rebuild (aka ALC reloading). You need to make your `CompositorTest` implement `ISerializationListener` to properly listen to reloading (before and after reloading).

The issue has been resolved after modifying your code to use the event functions from the ISerialization Listener.

One downside is that the `OnAfterDeserialize` only triggers when rebuilding, not on the project startup, so you won't see the red squares unless you build the C# project. Someone could have more knowledge and can educate me on this part.

```csharp
[Tool, GlobalClass]
public partial class CompositorTest : CompositorEffect, ISerializationListener
{
    void ISerializationListener.OnBeforeSerialize()
    {
        GD.Print("Unload Effects");
        if (_PointMultiMesh.IsValid) RS.FreeRid(_PointMultiMesh);
        if (_PointMultiMeshInst.IsValid) RS.FreeRid(_PointMultiMeshInst);
        if (_MeshRID.IsValid) RS.FreeRid(_MeshRID);
    }

    void ISerializationListener.OnAfterDeserialize()
    {
        GD.Print("Load Effects");
        EffectCallbackType = EffectCallbackTypeEnum.PostTransparent;
        RS.CallOnRenderThread(new Callable(this, MethodName._InitializeCompute));
    }
}
```
